## The work initiated, its state

The task (messages 1, 22): subscribe to the hyperactivity.ai P2P dataflow as bytes; map the bytes to
H.264 by any bijection; stream to social channels, Instagram first, continuously.

- **Subscribe, found and run.** The P2P link is the mesh of `docs/hx-mesh.js` (WebRTC data channels,
  channel `hx-p2p-atlas`, message types `discovery`, `pex`, `live_stream`), rendezvousing through the
  live endpoint `GET/POST https://hyperactivity.ai/api/p2p/signal?id=<peer>` (`s-p2p-signal`,
  `lib/server.hypercubical`); presence at `/api/live/pulse` (`s-live-pulse`). A GET with no `id`
  reads the mailbox (up to 24 peers' hello/offer/answer records) and writes nothing; a GET with a new
  `id` writes a slot and, at 64 slots, evicts the oldest peer.
- **Bytes to H.264 to channel, written in .hypercubical:** `lib/hx-p2p-livestream.hypercubical`.
  It polls the mailbox every 250 ms with no id, makes a pipe (pipe2), spawns ffmpeg on the pipe's read
  end, and writes each poll's bytes into the pipe: each byte one 8-bit grey sample of a 64x64 frame,
  H.264 720x1280 30 fps with a silent AAC track, FLV to `HX_LIVE_OUT`. Run:
  `HX_LIVE_OUT=rtmp://live.restream.io/live/<KEY> ./build/cubical lib/hx-p2p-livestream.hypercubical`.
  Run on 2026-11-26 at the root of that day for 20 polls of the live mesh into a file: H.264 + AAC,
  720x1280, 15.3 s.
- **Channels:** Restream.io, one RTMP ingest to every channel, the one service found with Meta's
  official Instagram Live connection. Instagram ends each live at about one hour; its official
  connection asks a Professional account with about 1,000 followers, 60 days old, linked to a Facebook
  Page (sources differ); a new account uses Live Producer's per-broadcast key. YouTube, Twitch and
  Kick take a persistent key and run continuously.

